        "id": "ch4_2-1",
        "text": "Introducing Python data containers\nPython supports several data types, both numeric as well as collections. Defining numeric\ndata types such as integers and floating-point numbers is based on assigning a value to\na variable. The value we assign to a variable determines the type of the numeric data\ntype. Note that a specific constructor (for example, int() and float() ) can also be\nused to create a variable of a specific data type. Container data types can also be defined\neither by assigning values in an appropriate format or by using a specific constructor for\neach collection data type. We will study five different container data types in this section:\nstrings , lists , tuples , dictionaries , and sets .\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Strings\n\u2022 Lists\n\u2022 Tuples\n\u2022 Dictionaries\n\u2022 Sets\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
